---
permalink: /llms.txt
template_engine: erb
layout: none
---
<%
  nav_groups = site.data.navigation.select(&:items)
  titles = nav_groups.flat_map(&:items).to_h { |item| [item.url, item.title] }
  titles["/writing/"] = "Writing"
  repeated_titles = titles.values.tally.select { |_, count| count > 1 }.keys + nav_groups.map(&:label)
  full_titles = nav_groups.flat_map { |group| group.items.map { |item| [item.url, repeated_titles.include?(item.title) ? "#{item.title} (#{group.label})" : titles[item.url]] } }.to_h
  resources = site.resources.to_h { |resource| [resource.relative_url, resource] }
  rules_by_id = site.data.rules.to_h { |rule| [rule.id, rule] }
  one_line = ->(s) { s.to_s.strip.gsub(/\s*\n\s*/, " ") }
  first_paragraph = ->(resource) {
    body = resource.respond_to?(:untransformed_content) ? resource.untransformed_content.to_s : resource.content.to_s
    body.split(/\n\s*\n/).map(&:strip).find { |block| !block.empty? && !block.start_with?("<", "#", "{", "|", "`", "-") }
  }
  summary_for = ->(url) {
    resource = resources[url]
    next "" unless resource
    one_line.(resource.data.summary || first_paragraph.(resource))
  }
  link_for = ->(url) {
    page_url, anchor = url.split("#", 2)
    title = (anchor && rules_by_id[anchor]&.name) || full_titles[page_url]
    "[#{title}](#{url})"
  }
-%>
# Uniform

> it's us studio's design system: a Tailwind v4 layer of theme tokens, components and one small script, with docs that explain every rule. The docs are written for people. This file routes agents to the pages that answer each task.

In a Rails app, add the `studio-uniform` gem, run `bin/rails uniform:install` to copy Uniform's Tailwind source into `app/assets/tailwind/uniform/`, import `./uniform/tailwind.css` after `tailwindcss`, link stylesheets with `stylesheet_link_tag :app` and load `uniform/uniform.js`, as [Install](/start/install/) shows. Run `uniform:install` again after each Uniform update; `bin/rails uniform:verify` fails in CI when the copy is stale. The script adds behaviour to a few components, and every component still works without it. Classes start with `u-`, tokens are Tailwind theme variables (`--background-color-surface`, `--text-color-muted`), and space uses `--spacing(n)`.

## Read first

<% ["/", "/start/rules/", "/writing/"].each do |url| -%>
- <%= raw link_for.(url) %>: <%= raw summary_for.(url) %>
<% end -%>

## Designing something new

When nothing in Uniform shows how to build it, read the rules for its section first and name the ones that apply. Design inside them. Never add a size, colour or weight that a rule doesn't name. Check [Reference](/start/reference/) for an existing piece first, and follow [No one-offs](/start/rules/#no-one-offs).

## Task routes

Read the pages for a task in the order listed.

<% site.data.task_routes.each do |route| -%>
- <%= raw route.title %>: <%= raw route.pages.map { |url| link_for.(url) }.join(", ") %>
<% end -%>

## Review checklist

Run this before calling a screen done. Take a screenshot at desktop width and at 390px, in light and dark, then check every rule below that has a Check line. Copy is checked against the studio's AI patterns checklist.

## All rules

Every rule, grouped by the page it lives on. Rules for copy live in the writing skill, summarized on [Writing style](/writing/).
<% site.data.rules.group_by(&:home).each do |rules_home, rules| -%>

### [<%= raw full_titles[rules_home] || titles[rules_home] %>](<%= rules_home %>)

<% rules.each do |rule| -%>
- [<%= raw rule.name %>](<%= rules_home %>#<%= rule.id %>): <%= raw one_line.(rule.summary) %><% if rule.check %> Check: <%= raw one_line.(rule.check) %><% end %>
<% end -%>
<% end -%>
<% nav_groups.each do |group| -%>

## <%= raw group.label %>

<% group.items.reject { |item| item.url == "/llms.txt" }.each do |item| -%>
- [<%= raw item.title %>](<%= item.url %>): <%= raw summary_for.(item.url) %>
<% end -%>
<% end -%>

## Class and element index

Every class and custom element, with the page it lives on.

<% site.data.classes.each do |entry| -%>
- `<%= raw entry.name %>`: [<%= raw full_titles[entry.page] || entry.page %>](<%= entry.page %>)
<% end -%>
<% site.data.elements.each do |element| -%>
- `<%= raw element.name %>`: [<%= raw full_titles[element.page.split("#").first] || element.page %>](<%= element.page %>)
<% end -%>
